          "error": null,
          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-741eafb403c21b977240a7bf",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-b7c7112f4fe90fa06bbd19ce",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-b7c7112f4fe90fa06bbd19ce",
          "source_text_sha256": "38e3203b8129d42662dbeeb77fedbbc4443cbd788a1b43e121314eefcad34c70",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On the evening of August 13, 2018, a resident of SAINT-THURIAU (56) was enjoying a clear sky to stargaze, when along a S/SO to N/NE axis, her gaze was drawn to a movement. She sees three bright points forming a triangle, at equal distance from each other, advancing at the same speed. Their brightness is that of the surrounding stars. The observation lasted about thirty seconds before he lost their trace in a blend of stars. Of weak strangeness and average consistency (single witness, but precise testimony), this case turns out to be the observation of a triplet of Yaogan 31 satellites (see the investigation report). \nAccording to the criteria of the GEIPAN, consistency is the amount of reliable and objective information gathered for a testimony. The witness's description of the PAN is perfectly characteristic of a triplet of satellites of the \"design\" NOSS (Naval Ocean Surveillance System) adopted by China (China's NOSS-Like Triplets) orbiting in formation: 3 faintly bright points moving together, isosceles triangle formation, apparent size of 10 cm, sky visible through the PAN, and apparent speed of approximately 0.5°/s (see NOSS Double and Triple Satellite Formations). During the time slot indicated by the witness, the Yaogan 31 triplet satellite passed on a trajectory corresponding to that of the PAN. The case is classified \"A\", observation of the Yaogan 31 satellite trio.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "2a36e464ddd761085a57f54145aef8fd1d6b54cc546016f6956fe14b663648b6"
        }
      ],
